Package: GFuse
Type: Package
Title: Graph-Guided Regularization for Order Estimation in Finite Mixture Models
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-05-28
Author: Peng Tang, Abbas Khalili, Archer Yang
Maintainer: Peng Tang <peng.tang@mail.mcgill.ca>
Description: Estimates the number of components (the order) of a finite mixture
    model and, just as importantly, provides an interpretable graph and
    solution-path representation of the fitted model for diagnosing the latent
    structure of heterogeneous data. An over-specified mixture is regularized
    along a graph built on the component atoms -- a mutual m-nearest-neighbour
    (m-NN) graph, a minimum spanning tree (MST), or the Group-Sort-Fuse (GSF)
    sorted chain. As the penalty strength increases, redundant components merge,
    tracing a solution path whose order of merges reveals a hierarchy of
    similarity among the underlying subpopulations. Gaussian, multivariate
    Student-t, multinomial, Poisson and exponential mixtures are supported. The
    method generalizes the Group-Sort-Fuse procedure of Manole and Khalili
    (2021) <doi:10.1214/21-AOS2102>.
License: GPL (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/ptang268/GFuse
BugReports: https://github.com/ptang268/GFuse/issues
LazyData: true
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppEigen
Imports: Rcpp (>= 0.12.10), mixtools, gtools, poLCA
